@title Landing zone network layout
@subtitle Alderwood Health Analytics, AWS us-east-2
@author Cloud team
@date 2026-10-09
@width wide

## Overview

Three AWS accounts are joined by a transit gateway. All internet-bound traffic is inspected before it leaves, and a Direct Connect link runs back to our Columbus data center.

!! **Staging may never route to prod.** This is the rule auditors ask about. See Routing rules below.

## Network diagram

diagram net dir=LR title="us-east-2 landing zone network"
net: tgw "Transit Gateway" svc focus
net: fw "Network Firewall" svc focus
net: nat "NAT Gateway" svc
net: api "Claims API" svc "ECS"
net: db "Claims DB" db "Aurora"
net: stgapi "Claims API Staging" svc
net: dc "Columbus Data Center" ext "2 x 1 Gbps"
net: internet "Internet" ext
net: group inspvpc "Inspection VPC 10.0.0.0/16" fw, nat
net: group netacct "Network account" tgw, inspvpc
net: group claimsvpc "Claims VPC 10.10.0.0/16" api, db
net: group prodacct "Prod account" claimsvpc
net: group stgvpc "Staging VPC 10.20.0.0/16" stgapi
net: group stgacct "Staging account" stgvpc
net: claimsvpc -> tgw : attachment
net: stgvpc -> tgw : attachment
net: tgw -> inspvpc : egress inspection
net: inspvpc -> internet : via NAT
net: dc -> tgw : Direct Connect
net: api -> db : port 5432

## Address plan

table = VPC,account,CIDR,subnet layout; Inspection VPC,Network,10.0.0.0/16,2 firewall subnets and 2 NAT subnets; Claims VPC,Prod,10.10.0.0/16,3 private app subnets and 3 data subnets; Staging VPC,Staging,10.20.0.0/16,2 private app subnets and 2 data subnets

## Routing rules

!!! **Staging may never route to prod.** The Staging VPC must have no route to the Claims VPC through the transit gateway or any other path.

- No internet gateways in workload VPCs. Internet-bound traffic leaves only through the Inspection VPC.
- The Direct Connect link from the Columbus Data Center reaches prod only.
